  "conclusion": "Confirmed retained11-26 equal-work defect in selector continuation, already corrected by common expanded-call target preservation. Historical fast native numbers cannot be assumed equivalent work. No new performance patch justified by recovering the skipped path.",
  "limits": [
    "Exact11-23 installed native bytes/link plan remain unavailable; this is an11-26 retained-input witness, not a substitute capture.",
    "The frozen runner recursively loads its policy directory; standard datagram/TCP policies have selectors. When a configured selector is processed from curr0, curr becomes1 and1>selectors is false for any selectors>=1, so CONTINUE is required. Other early errors/rejects remain possible.",
    "Source and native-code evidence proves the skipped continuation path for admissible standard-policy inputs. It does not count actual historical branch hits or attribute exactly261.898ns to that branch.",
    "The4replays preserve all nonbranch operations (one internal RIP target relocation normalized per filter) and external target sequences. No guest/timing/old linker export or production change occurred."
  ]
